<!--
  RUT_Miasma_HardenedImmunity.xml      UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M5 build pass

  miasma_kit_spec.md M5's own table, 30% tier: "RUT_HardenedImmunity_<disease>
  (immunity-gain-speed / disease-resist stat offsets, per-disease flavor)."
  One per vanilla disease RUT_Miasma_ForgeOnSurvival.xml patches
  HediffCompProperties_ForgeOnSurvival onto (Flu, Animal_Flu, Plague,
  Animal_Plague, Malaria, SleepingSickness, WoundInfection) - a pawn who
  survives THAT disease in the Miasma can only ever roll THAT disease's own
  hardened immunity, never another's (the per-disease list-membership does
  the "flavor," not a shared pool).

  Stats confirmed real against the live 1.6/Odyssey decompile
  (RimWorld/StatDefOf.cs), not guessed:
    ImmunityGainSpeed       "The speed at which this character gains
                             immunity to diseases." defaultBaseValue 1,
                             PercentZero - a statOffset here is additive
                             percentage points.
    ImmunityGainSpeedFactor exists too (Building category, a multiplier
                             stat) but ImmunityGainSpeed alone already reads
                             correctly as "immunity-gain-speed" per the
                             spec's own words, so only that one is used -
                             stacking both would double-count the same
                             English phrase as two different mechanisms.
  No standalone "disease resistance" StatDef exists in the indexed 1.6
  source; ImmunityGainSpeed is the real, closest, and only lever the spec's
  own phrase maps onto - not invented.

  Permanent (isBad false, no removal comp): recovering from a real fight
  with the disease is what earns this, and it never goes away, matching the
  fever-forged framing ("something it leaves behind").

  Offset magnitude +0.20 (20 percentage points) is this pass's own INVENTED
  tuning value - noticeable without trivializing a second bout.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_HardenedImmunity_Flu</defName>
    <label>flu-hardened</label>
    <description>The fever that should have killed you taught your body something instead. You shake off a fresh dose of flu faster than you used to.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <ImmunityGainSpeed>0.20</ImmunityGainSpeed>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

